# mode-select.script - the game's own path to a display mode.
#
# Replayed by the `mode` verb, once. It starts at the MAIN MENU and ends back
# there, having advanced the screen resolution by one step in the game's own
# options screen.
#
# ONE step is enough because the verb restricts what is offered before
# replaying this: the list becomes 640x480x8, 640x480x16 and the mode asked
# for, so the single click below moves from the resolution the front end is
# already in to the only other one on offer. Both boot depths stay because the
# front end runs at 640x480 in both and a list missing either is refused - and
# this game does not check a refusal.
#
# The game recreates its surfaces itself; nothing here resizes anything. That
# is the whole reason the path exists rather than a host-side call.
#
# WHERE THE COORDINATES COME FROM
#
# Recovered by headless discovery runs through build/recomp/pop_smoke, one
# click at a time, each confirmed by the frame it produced. The frames are kept
# in build/recomp/mode-select-evidence/ and named below.
#
#   OPTIONS at (320, 260): the main menu's fifth action row. The rows are 30 apart
#     from New Game at y 140, so Options is 140 + 4*30 = 260, and the click
#     produced 01-options-screen.ppm - the GAME tab, with TOOLTIPS, ROTATION,
#     FLIP ROTATION, STAY SELECTED and AUTOCAST SPELL, and the tab row GAME /
#     SOUND / GRAPHICS above BACK.
#   GRAPHICS at (470, 435): the third tab in that row, measured off
#     01-options-screen.ppm. The click produced 02-graphics-tab.ppm - SCREEN
#     RESOLUTION, SKY, FOOTSTEPS, LANDSCAPE DETAIL, QUICK DEFAULTS, and
#     DIRECT3D OPTIONS.
#   The resolution's right arrow at (538, 152): the closing bracket of
#     "SCREEN RESOLUTION : <640 X 480>", measured off 02-graphics-tab.ppm.
#     One click advanced it to 800 X 600, which is 03- and 04- either side.
#   BACK at (320, 466): under the tab row, measured off 02-graphics-tab.ppm.
#
# WHY `click` AND NOT `guestclick`
#
# `guestclick` places the pointer and this game ignores where it is placed: a
# guestclick at New Game's row selected MULTIPLAYER instead, the row under the
# game's own cursor. Populous hit-tests against the pointer IT integrates from
# relative motion, so a script that needs a particular row has to walk the
# game's cursor there. That is what the corner pin and `moveby` below do, the
# same technique level1.script uses and for the same reason.
#
# WHEN THE MODE ACTUALLY TAKES EFFECT, WHICH IS NOT WHERE IT IS CHOSEN
#
# Leaving the options screen does NOT change the display mode. Measured: after
# choosing 800 X 600 and clicking BACK, the host was still at 640x480x8, and it
# was still at 640x480 after New Game, the tutorial prompt and the whole level
# select screen. The mode changed only when a level started and the game
# recreated its surfaces - 05-level-at-800x600.ppm, and the run's own summary
# in 06-run-that-reached-800x600.log reads "display mode: 800x600 16bpp" with
# 240436 draws at it.
#
# So a script cannot assert the mode when this path ends. It has to enter a
# level first. The `mode` verb has no timeout for that reason: it arms the
# claim, and the run fails at the end if the mode never arrived.

moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 260
wait 700
click left 320 260
wait 4000

moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 470 435
wait 700
click left 470 435
wait 4000

# One step along the offered list. The list is whatever the shim offers, which
# the `mode` verb restricts before replaying this.
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 538 152
wait 700
click left 538 152
wait 3000

moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 466
wait 700
click left 320 466
wait 5000
